meta {
  name: Update Lab Test
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/lab-tests/{{labTestId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "testDisplayName": "CBC (Complete Blood Count)",
    "priceMaximum": 600,
    "commissionPrice": 60,
    "remarks": "Q3 price revision",
    "reportingTimeFrom": "09:00",
    "reportingTimeTo": "17:00",
    "approvalDurationMinValue": 30,
    "approvalDurationMinUnit": "MINUTES",
    "approvalDurationMaxValue": 2,
    "approvalDurationMaxUnit": "HOURS",
    "branchId":"c1a13dd2-6562-446c-83ca-4f0220976134"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 07dc5e99-4aee-46d8-917d-d43a25745017
  labTestId: 3fd4f5ca-f3b3-4ac8-b86c-adab2280386a
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__update_test` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Patch a lab test's core fields (send only what changes). `versionHistory` is
  never edited here (use Add Version).

  Includes the Reporting window / Approval duration pair (SRS §5.4/§5.5):
  `reportingTimeFrom`/`reportingTimeTo` ("HH:mm", signatory-availability
  window) and `approvalDurationMinValue`/`MinUnit`/`MaxValue`/`MaxUnit`
  (expected approval turnaround, value+unit — distinct from the existing
  `approvalTimeFrom`/`approvalTimeTo` time-of-day window).
  
  Child sets are REPLACED when provided: include a full `samples` array and/or
  `resultParams` array (each param with its `referenceRanges`/`referenceValues`)
  to swap the whole set, in one transaction. Omit a child array to leave it untouched.

  **Parameters keep their identity.** Send each existing parameter's `id` (the one
  `Get Lab Test` returned): the server updates THAT parameter, so renaming its
  `parameterCode` keeps every result already entered for it. Without an `id` a
  parameter is matched by `parameterCode` (case-insensitive), as before; an `id` that
  is not a live parameter of this test is ignored, and the same `id` twice is a 422.
  **Notes are cleaned on save.** The HTML is cleaned of anything active before it is stored: <script>, <style>, <iframe>,
  event-handler attributes (onerror=…), javascript:/data: links and CSS that loads a URL are removed; formatting
  (bold, lists, tables, colours, alignment, links, images) is kept. What the API returns is the cleaned text, and
  the length limit applies to it. This applies to usefulFor, interpretationOfResults, limitations, remarks and references (a parameter's own `notes` is plain text and is not rich text).

  A parameter that nothing matches is created (a client `id` is never used as the new
  row's id); an existing parameter that is not sent is soft-deleted.

  **Clearing a parameter's Note.** A matched parameter is patched in place, and only the
  fields you send are written: an omitted `notes` leaves the stored Note as it is. To clear
  it send `"notes": ""` (or whitespace) — a blank Note is stored as NULL, never as an empty
  string. A branch picks the change up on its next "Import Master Data". The same blank-to-NULL
  rule applies when a parameter is created (Create Lab Test, or a new parameter in an update).

  **Reference ranges keep their rows when unchanged.** A range with the same analyzer,
  method, unit, gender, age band, lower/upper limit, critical limits and abnormal-flag
  style as a live one keeps that row and its id (a report that picked it still points at
  a live range); only the Default flag and the Display text are patched in place. A
  changed or removed range is soft-deleted (its old row stays, frozen, for the reports
  that used it) and a changed or added one is created. Reference values are still fully
  replaced.

  **Same key, different limits is allowed** (Copy a range and change only its limits):
  two ranges with the same analyzer, method, unit, gender and age band are accepted when
  their lower or upper limit differs (compared to 4 decimals). Such a set needs exactly
  one `isDefault: true` among them (422 "Mark a Default range…" / "Only one range can be
  Default…"). Identical limits are 422 "A similar reference range already exists…", and a
  partial Gender/Age overlap is still 422 "Overlapping reference range…". The Excel import
  keeps refusing a same-key pair.

  Same cross-field rules and conflicts as Create (422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`, 409 on
  name/code/parameterCode). 404 `LAB_TEST_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other tenant.

  **TAT propagation (Branch Master Data only):** when `:masterDataId` is a
  branch's master data, the test's resulting TAT (`tatMinValue`/`tatMinUnit`/
  `tatMaxValue`/`tatMaxUnit`) is pushed, in the same transaction, to its
  Lab Test List copies in **every** list of the branch (Walk-in + PT-category/referral
  lists; user duplicates excluded) — the rows Create Order's Diagnostic Items and
  the TAT engine read. A copy is updated only when its TAT is empty or still equals
  the previous master TAT; a TAT customised in the Lab Test List is kept. Tenant Master
  Data edits reach the branch via **Import Master Data from Tenant**.
}
